    "result": {"data":{"markdownRemark":{"html":"<p>The best trip of my life is officially over.</p>\n<p>And what didn't it have! Starting from the absolutely delicious multi-cuisine food, to the jaw dropping views, and the captivating experiences -- I had all I could ask for in seven days. To top things off, the trip couldn't be with anyone better -- than the love of my life.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 700px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/aa65fc0f71edd4ce7000cc3f9aef7002/09b5b/cover.jpg\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 177.7142857142857%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/jpeg;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Hola!\"\n        title=\"Hola!\"\n        src=\"/static/aa65fc0f71edd4ce7000cc3f9aef7002/03346/cover.jpg\"\n        srcset=\"/static/aa65fc0f71edd4ce7000cc3f9aef7002/71299/cover.jpg 175w,\n/static/aa65fc0f71edd4ce7000cc3f9aef7002/1e9fe/cover.jpg 350w,\n/static/aa65fc0f71edd4ce7000cc3f9aef7002/03346/cover.jpg 700w,\n/static/aa65fc0f71edd4ce7000cc3f9aef7002/c3223/cover.jpg 1050w,\n/static/aa65fc0f71edd4ce7000cc3f9aef7002/da6ee/cover.jpg 1400w,\n/static/aa65fc0f71edd4ce7000cc3f9aef7002/09b5b/cover.jpg 2268w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>It feels nice to write this blog. It has only been about a month -- the rush has faded, life has settled, and now it's time to make congeal my memories.</p>\n<h1>Day 1</h1>\n<p>Our trip to the jewel of the east started rather awkwardly. Our US Bangla flight was (un)fortunately delayed by four hours. I remember my travel agent, Mr Manoj calling me at the dead of the morning at 1:30. Great news it seemed, as I had little sleep from having to go through my travel checklist unncessarily -- I always lack confidence in my ability to arrange things without hiccups.</p>","frontmatter":{"title":"Malaysia","description":"Truly Asia","date":"2024-06-06","slug":"/blog/malaysia","tags":["Malaysia","Honeymoon"]}}},"pageContext":{}},
